## Claim under pressure
SPRINT **7.10** (HIGH): `c_parse_secret_env` tags line-start `// SECRET: <ident>`
into `__sec__name=1` / `__secref__name=1`. Path-A memory close replaces
per-char `name = name + c` with one `str_slice`. Zero-trust gates for
**this** close (not 7.1 walker, not 7.2 last-arg):

| # | Gate | Expectation |
|---|------|-------------|
| Z1 | Slice must not drop / truncate SECRET names | Tagged name == full ident span; sink refuse spells that full name |
| Z2 | Must not fail-open empty ident | `// SECRET:` with no ident → `ERR\tsecret\tinvalid name` + rc≠0 |
| Z3 | Non-line-start `SECRET:` is not a directive | Mid-line / string / indent / `//SECRET:` / case-fold must not tag |
| Z4 | Do not reopen 7.1 / 7.2 | Walker + last-arg stay closed; this audit does not retarget them |

Adversarial stance: treat exclusive-end off-by-one, a C stack cap, and
`oo_str_slice` OOB→`""` as **truncate / drop weapons**. Treat any skip of
`name == ""` as **fail-open**. Treat any `SECRET:` not at column-0 after
`\n` (or file start) as a **false directive** until proved ignored.

